{
  "description": "Public origins and the htu of DPoP proofs, SPEC-v0.md section 11.7 items 1 and 6. A case with value: whether the configured value is a public origin (valid or invalid): https://, a DNS name of at least two labels of lower-case letters, digits and hyphens, every label that begins with xn-- decoding with Punycode (RFC 3492) to a label with a character outside ASCII and encoding back to itself, no IDNA applied (an implementation MAY apply it to a value it is configured with, Section 11.7 item 1, but no case depends on it), the last label with a letter and not 0x followed by hexadecimal digits only, no final dot, the port only if it is not 443, nothing after host and port. A case with htu and url: whether the htu of a proof matches the URL the implementation built from its public origin, both normalized as RFC 3986 sections 6.2.2 and 6.2.3 describe (case of scheme and host, percent-encoding, dot segments, default port, empty path) and without query and fragment (RFC 9449 section 4.3); a value that is not an absolute URL with a host, or has a broken percent-encoding, matches nothing. A case with proof and request: whether a DPoP proof is valid for the request (valid or invalid). proof gives the header members typ and alg, the RFC 7638 thumbprint jkt of the proof's key, and the claims htm, htu, iat, jti and ath; request gives the method, the url the implementation built from its public origin, the time the request was received, and either the access_token with the thumbprint bound_jkt of the key the token is bound to, or the dpop_jkt of the authorization request at the token endpoint. seen lists jti values accepted before within the window; started, if present, is the start of a process whose memory of jti values does not survive a restart. Times are seconds since the epoch. A proof is valid if typ is dpop+jwt; alg is an asymmetric algorithm the implementation offers (ES256 in these cases), never none or a MAC; htm is the method, compared exactly; htu matches as in the htu cases; iat lies at most 60 seconds before and at most 10 seconds after received, bounds included; jti is not in seen; with started, iat is later than started plus 10 seconds; with an access token, ath is the SHA-256 of the token in base64url without padding and jkt is bound_jkt; at the token endpoint with dpop_jkt, jkt is dpop_jkt.",
  "cases": [
    {"id": "o01", "section": "11.7", "value": "https://home.example.net", "expected": "valid", "why": "a DNS name of three labels"},
    {"id": "o02", "section": "11.7", "value": "https://hm.example.org:8443", "expected": "valid", "why": "a port other than 443"},
    {"id": "o03", "section": "11.7", "value": "https://xn--bcher-kva.example", "expected": "valid", "why": "an A-label"},
    {"id": "o04", "section": "11.7", "value": "https://k7q2xwmpd4hj3n6rt5vbyc2ezu.homes.example.net", "expected": "valid", "why": "a standard name of a relay"},
    {"id": "o05", "section": "11.7", "value": "https://1a.example", "expected": "valid", "why": "digits in a label that is not the last"},
    {"id": "o06", "section": "11.7", "value": "https://home.example.net:1", "expected": "valid", "why": "the lowest port"},
    {"id": "o07", "section": "11.7", "value": "https://home.example.net:65535", "expected": "valid", "why": "the highest port"},
    {"id": "o08", "section": "11.7", "value": "http://home.example.net", "expected": "invalid", "why": "the scheme http"},
    {"id": "o09", "section": "11.7", "value": "HTTPS://home.example.net", "expected": "invalid", "why": "the scheme in upper case"},
    {"id": "o10", "section": "11.7", "value": "https://Home.example.net", "expected": "invalid", "why": "the host in upper case"},
    {"id": "o11", "section": "11.7", "value": "https://home.example.net/", "expected": "invalid", "why": "a path of a single slash"},
    {"id": "o12", "section": "11.7", "value": "https://home.example.net/mcp", "expected": "invalid", "why": "a path"},
    {"id": "o13", "section": "11.7", "value": "https://home.example.net?x=1", "expected": "invalid", "why": "a query"},
    {"id": "o14", "section": "11.7", "value": "https://home.example.net#top", "expected": "invalid", "why": "a fragment"},
    {"id": "o15", "section": "11.7", "value": "https://admin@home.example.net", "expected": "invalid", "why": "userinfo"},
    {"id": "o16", "section": "11.7", "value": "https://home.example.net:443", "expected": "invalid", "why": "the default port written out"},
    {"id": "o17", "section": "11.7", "value": "https://home.example.net:", "expected": "invalid", "why": "an empty port"},
    {"id": "o18", "section": "11.7", "value": "https://home.example.net:08443", "expected": "invalid", "why": "a port with a leading zero"},
